## ud8.10
ud8.10:1.1 | S: So I have heard. | T: I have heard that
ud8.10:1.2 | S: At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. | T: on one occasion the Blessed One was staying near Sāvatthī at Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery.
ud8.10:1.3 | S: There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, | T: There he addressed the monks,
ud8.10:1.4 | S: “Mendicants!” | T: “Monks!”
ud8.10:1.5 | S: “Venerable sir,” they replied. | T: “Yes, lord,” the monks responded to him.
ud8.10:1.6 | S: The Buddha said this: | T: The Blessed One said,
ud8.10:2.1 | S: “Mendicants, when Dabba the Mallian rose into the air and, sitting cross-legged in midair, entered and withdrew from the fire element before becoming fully quenched, his body burning and combusting left neither ashes nor soot to be found. | T: “When Dabba Mallaputta rose up into the air and, sitting cross-legged in the sky, in space, entered & emerged from the fire property and was totally unbound, his body burned and was consumed so that neither ashes nor soot could be discerned.
ud8.10:2.2 | S: It’s like when ghee or oil blaze and burn, and neither ashes nor soot are found. | T: Just as when ghee or oil is burned and consumed, neither ashes nor soot can be discerned,
ud8.10:2.3 | S: In the same way, when Dabba the Mallian rose into the air and, sitting cross-legged in midair, entered and withdrew from the fire element before becoming fully quenched, his body burning and combusting left neither ashes nor soot to be found.” | T: in the same way, when Dabba Mallaputta rose up into the air and, sitting cross-legged in the sky, in space, entered & emerged from the fire property and was totally unbound, his body burned and was consumed so that neither ashes nor soot could be discerned.”
ud8.10:3.1 | S: Then, understanding this matter, on that occasion the Buddha expressed this heartfelt sentiment: | T: Then, on realizing the significance of that, the Blessed One on that occasion exclaimed:
ud8.10:4.1 | S: “Just as the glow of iron struck | T: Just as the destination of a glowing fire
ud8.10:4.2 | S: by a hammer in the fire of Jātaveda | T: struck with a [blacksmith’s] iron hammer,
ud8.10:4.3 | S: gradually dissipates, | T: gradually growing calm,
ud8.10:4.4 | S: its destiny unknown; | T: isn’t known:
ud8.10:5.1 | S: in the same way, for the rightly released, | T: Even so, there’s no destination to describe for those rightly released
ud8.10:5.2 | S: who have crossed the flood of sensual bonds, | T: –having crossed over the flood of sensuality’s bond–
ud8.10:5.3 | S: there is no destination to describe— | T: (none)
ud8.10:5.4 | S: they have found unshakable happiness.” | T: for those who’ve attained unwavering bliss.
ud8.10:5.5 | P: Dasamaṁ. | T: (none)
ud8.10:5.6 | P: Pāṭaligāmiyavaggo aṭṭhamo. | T: (none)

